1
00:00:07,897 --> 00:00:13,126
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,374 --> 00:00:15,249
by Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki

3
00:00:16,053 --> 00:00:23,030
اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراَّ

4
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:24,149
 اَمَّا بَعْدْ

5
00:00:24,323 --> 00:00:26,577
السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

6
00:00:29,063 --> 00:00:34,863
As we mentioned earlier, the Muslims were not allowed to fight in the beginning,

7
00:00:35,271 --> 00:00:35,886
the command was

8
00:00:35,926 --> 00:00:38,402
  اِصْبِرُوْ فَاِنِّيْ لَمْ اُؤمَرْ بِقِتَالْ

9
00:00:38,442 --> 00:00:40,082
I'm not given permission to fight,

10
00:00:42,249 --> 00:00:44,082
 and they were wronged.

11
00:00:45,495 --> 00:00:50,562
We talked about all of the forms of oppression that the Muslims suffered from, in Makkah.

12
00:00:50,966 --> 00:00:56,181
We covered that part in the talks of the Makkah period.

13
00:00:57,180 --> 00:01:01,680
They used all various forms of aggression against the Muslims.

14
00:01:02,656 --> 00:01:06,340
Now for the Arabs to be restrained from fighting wasn't easy,

15
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:15,194
you know, these are tribesmen they didn't have a heritage or an anti war movement at that time,

16
00:01:15,559 --> 00:01:18,051
they didn't have any peace activists, in those days

17
00:01:18,361 --> 00:01:21,047
they didn't have the likes of Martin Luther King or Gandhi,

18
00:01:21,087 --> 00:01:25,428
I mean, a tribesman, if you transgress against him, he is going to fight back.

19
00:01:26,175 --> 00:01:32,007
So, for them to be restrained from fighting back and avenging for what happened to them, was very difficult,

20
00:01:32,626 --> 00:01:34,460
but it was a test of their patience.

21
00:01:35,311 --> 00:01:39,671
And that's why Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying اِصْبِرُوْ be patient, so it was testing them.

22
00:01:40,047 --> 00:01:43,680
But For example, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

23
00:01:43,931 --> 00:01:45,962
وَلَقَدْ عَلِمْتُ اَنَّه’سَيَكُوْنُ قِتَالْ

24
00:01:46,256 --> 00:01:49,184
I knew that there's going to be fighting, ultimately we're going to have to fight,

25
00:01:49,335 --> 00:01:52,916
there's no way to get out of this difficult situation, we're in.

26
00:01:53,075 --> 00:01:55,472
 Except by fighting in the path of Allah.

27
00:01:56,371 --> 00:01:59,290
So, he knew that it was coming along.

28
00:02:00,623 --> 00:02:07,645
The permission was given during the early days of Madina, some say it was given before Hijrah(هجرة),

29
00:02:08,010 --> 00:02:12,624
but the actual practice of it didn't happen, except in Madina.

30
00:02:13,654 --> 00:02:20,827
Now to fight against the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, demanded preparation.

31
00:02:21,406 --> 00:02:28,010
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was now preparing the Muslim community and training it.

32
00:02:28,582 --> 00:02:31,272
And this training took two forms,

33
00:02:31,679 --> 00:02:36,790
One was spiritual training, and the second was physical training or preparation.

34
00:02:38,145 --> 00:02:43,985
So, this would lead us into the fourth project, which is the establishment of the Muslim army.

35
00:02:44,025 --> 00:02:46,212
We talked about the establishment of the Masjid(مسجد).

36
00:02:46,503 --> 00:02:49,323
we talked about brotherhood and we talked about the covenant

37
00:02:49,363 --> 00:02:52,169
and now number four, the establishment of the army.

38
00:02:52,564 --> 00:02:58,328
Now to state it that way, the establishment of the army isn't really, very accurate

39
00:02:58,423 --> 00:03:01,486
because there weren't any professional soldiers.

40
00:03:01,526 --> 00:03:04,113
This wasn't a professional army, it was more of a militia.

41
00:03:05,224 --> 00:03:09,914
The linguistic definition of the word militia would fit the situation more.

42
00:03:10,286 --> 00:03:17,339
It says in the American dictionary a militia is citizens army, as distinct from a body of professional soldiers.

43
00:03:17,379 --> 00:03:21,236
So there weren't any professional soldiers, in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

44
00:03:21,665 --> 00:03:28,259
Everyone who fulfilled five requirements, was expected to participate in Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

45
00:03:28,299 --> 00:03:30,837
 and these five requirements were, Islam, that's number one.

46
00:03:31,125 --> 00:03:34,318
Number two, Baloogh(بلوغ) the age of puberty.

47
00:03:34,577 --> 00:03:37,297
Number three, Al-Aql(ألعقل) sanity.

48
00:03:37,595 --> 00:03:41,603
Number four, Assalamah Min-Al-Oyub(ألسلامة من العيوب)  to be free of defects

49
00:03:41,976 --> 00:03:47,120
that would prevent a person from being able to participate, such as being blind, or handicapped.

50
00:03:47,527 --> 00:03:50,446
And number five, financial ability.

51
00:03:50,906 --> 00:03:56,161
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ didn't have the ability to sponsor every fighter,

52
00:03:56,351 --> 00:04:00,700
like a government would sponsor its army, they had to finance themselves.

53
00:04:01,422 --> 00:04:09,173
Also, it says that the militia is the whole body of physically fit male civilians legible by law for military service.

54
00:04:09,993 --> 00:04:14,938
So, the word militia suits it more than the word army.

55
00:04:16,419 --> 00:04:18,951
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was preparing them spiritually,

56
00:04:19,912 --> 00:04:22,539
and Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an were also preparing them for that,

57
00:04:22,610 --> 00:04:26,975
for example, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says, Surat-Ut-Toba(سورة التوبة) verse 111, and 112

58
00:04:27,211 --> 00:04:34,811
إِنَّ اللَّهَ اشْتَرَىٰ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَنْفُسَهُمْ وَأَمْوَالَهُمْ

59
00:04:35,113 --> 00:04:40,128
وَأَمْوَالَهُمْ بِأَنَّ لَهُمُ الْجَنَّةَ ۚ

60
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:47,455
يُقَاتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ فَيَقْتُلُونَ وَيُقْتَلُونَ ۖ

61
00:04:47,852 --> 00:04:55,935
وَعْدًا عَلَيْهِ حَقًّا فِي التَّوْرَاةِ وَالْإِنْجِيلِ وَالْقُرْآنِ ۚ

62
00:04:56,228 --> 00:05:00,588
وَمَنْ أَوْفَىٰ بِعَهْدِهِ مِنَ اللَّهِ ۚ

63
00:05:00,898 --> 00:05:06,327
فَاسْتَبْشِرُوا بِبَيْعِكُمُ الَّذِي بَايَعْتُمْ بِهِ ۚ

64
00:05:06,652 --> 00:05:11,128
وَذَٰلِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيمُ۝

65
00:05:11,412 --> 00:05:19,344
Indeed Allah has purchase from the believers, their lives and their properties, in exchange for that, they will have paradise.

66
00:05:19,876 --> 00:05:23,401
They fight in the cause of Allah, so they kill and are killed.

67
00:05:23,647 --> 00:05:28,811
It is a true promise binding upon Him in the Torah(توراة), and the Gospel and the Qur'an

68
00:05:29,081 --> 00:05:31,541
and who is truer to his covenant than Allah.

69
00:05:31,859 --> 00:05:34,983
So, rejoice in your transaction which you have contracted

70
00:05:35,129 --> 00:05:38,279
and it is that which is the great attainment.

71
00:05:39,851 --> 00:05:41,628
Allah is teaching them to be patient.

72
00:05:42,298 --> 00:05:48,934
إِنْ يَمْسَسْكُمْ قَرْحٌ فَقَدْ مَسَّ الْقَوْمَ قَرْحٌ مِثْلُهُ ۚ

73
00:05:49,244 --> 00:05:54,284
وَتِلْكَ الْأَيَّامُ نُدَاوِلُهَا بَيْنَ النَّاسِ

74
00:05:54,562 --> 00:06:03,005
وَلِيَعْلَمَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَيَتَّخِذَ مِنْكُمْ شُهَدَاءَ

75
00:06:03,289 --> 00:06:07,600
 وَاللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الظَّالِمِينَ۝

76
00:06:07,894 --> 00:06:16,337
وَلِيُمَحِّصَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَيَمْحَقَ الْكَافِرِينَ۝

77
00:06:16,858 --> 00:06:29,611
أَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ أَنْ تَدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ وَلَمَّا يَعْلَمِ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ جَاهَدُوا مِنْكُمْ وَيَعْلَمَ الصَّابِرِينَ۝

78
00:06:30,542 --> 00:06:36,762
If a wound should touch you, there has already touched the opposing people, a wound similar to it.

79
00:06:37,134 --> 00:06:43,132
And these days of varying conditions, We alternate among the people, one day you win, one day you lose.

80
00:06:44,075 --> 00:06:51,024
So, that Allah may make evident those who believe and may take to Himself from among you, martyrs.

81
00:06:51,468 --> 00:06:53,651
And Allah does not like the wrongdoers.

82
00:06:54,095 --> 00:06:58,555
And that Allah may purify the believers through trials and destroy the disbelievers.

83
00:06:59,470 --> 00:07:06,776
Or do you think that you will enter Paradise,  while Allah has not yet made evident, those of you who fight in His cause

84
00:07:07,030 --> 00:07:10,408
 And make evident those who are steadfast.

85
00:07:10,858 --> 00:07:15,181
And you had certainly wished for death, martyrdom, before you encountered it.

86
00:07:15,475 --> 00:07:19,007
And you have now seen it, before you, while you were looking on.

87
00:07:19,456 --> 00:07:25,075
So, these are examples of Ayaat(آيات) in which Allahعَزّوجَلّ was preparing the Muslims.

88
00:07:25,369 --> 00:07:30,279
Examples of Ahadith(احاديث) in Bukhari(بخاريْ) narrated by Abu Hurairah رضي الله عنه.

89
00:07:30,319 --> 00:07:32,453
A man came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

90
00:07:32,984 --> 00:07:36,215
يا رَسُوْل الله دُلَّنِيْ عَلَى عَمَلٍ يَعْدِلُ الْجِهَادْ

91
00:07:36,628 --> 00:07:40,715
O Rasool Ullah tell me about something that is as virtuous as Jihad(جهاد).

92
00:07:41,016 --> 00:07:43,016
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I can't find any.

93
00:07:43,358 --> 00:07:45,165
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told the man;

94
00:07:45,633 --> 00:07:48,840
When the Mujahid(مجاهد) goes out in the path of Allah,

95
00:07:49,157 --> 00:07:57,416
can you enter your mosque, and pray continuously without any rest and fast continuously without breaking your fast.

96
00:07:57,781 --> 00:07:59,559
So, the man said and who could do that?

97
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:05,538
Meaning that the reward of the Mujahid(مجاهد) is greater than fasting continuously and praying continuously.

98
00:08:06,376 --> 00:08:10,564
So, the fighting of the disbelievers is more virtuous than Jihad Un Nafs(جهاد النفس)

99
00:08:10,802 --> 00:08:13,818
because praying and fasting is part of Jihad(جهاد) Un Nafs(جهاد النفس)

100
00:08:13,898 --> 00:08:19,021
and Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying here that if a person is praying continuously and fasting continuously

101
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:24,389
they cannot receive the rewards of somebody who went out to fight in the path of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

102
00:08:24,846 --> 00:08:27,069
When they were coming back from the Ghazwah(غزوة) of Tabook(تبوك)

103
00:08:27,133 --> 00:08:29,609
Rasool Allah ﷺ told my Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذ ابن جبل);

104
00:08:29,932 --> 00:08:34,493
اِنْ شِئْتَ اأنبأتُكَ بِرَاْسِ الْاَمْرِيْ وَعَمُوْدِهِ و ذرْوَة سِنَامِهِ

105
00:08:35,103 --> 00:08:37,134
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذ ابن جبل),

106
00:08:37,174 --> 00:08:43,228
if you want I will tell you about the head of the affair, its pillar and its peak.

107
00:08:43,656 --> 00:08:50,274
The head of the affair is Islam, and its pillar is Salah(صلاة), and its peak is Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

108
00:08:50,375 --> 00:08:55,662
so the most virtuous act the peak of Islam is fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله عَزّوجَلّ).

109
00:08:56,090 --> 00:08:58,674
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in a Hadith(حديث) in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(المسلم);

110
00:08:58,889 --> 00:09:01,349
وَاعْلَمُوْا اَنَّ الْجَنَّةَ تَحْتَ ظِلَالِ السُّيُوْفْ

111
00:09:01,615 --> 00:09:05,465
Realized that Paradise is under the shade of swords.

112
00:09:05,751 --> 00:09:08,100
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(المسلم)

113
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:13,496
مَنْ جهَّزَ غَازِيًا في سبيلِ اللَّهِ فَقَدْ غَزَا، ومنْ خَلَفَ غَازيًا في أَهْلِهِ بخَيْر فَقَدْ غزَا

114
00:09:14,392 --> 00:09:17,248
Whoever finances a fighter in the path of Allah has fought,

115
00:09:17,668 --> 00:09:22,509
And whoever takes care of the family of a fighter has fought,

116
00:09:22,731 --> 00:09:27,501
the reward of Ribat(رباط) which is being stationed in the path of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

117
00:09:27,752 --> 00:09:31,406
رِبَاطُ يَوْمٍ وَلَيْلَةٍ خَيْرٌ مِنْ صِيَامِ شَهْرٍ وَقِيَامِهِ ،

118
00:09:31,912 --> 00:09:33,452
This is Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم)

119
00:09:33,690 --> 00:09:39,612
Ribaat(رباط) for one day in the path of Allah is better than fasting entire month and praying that month.

120
00:09:41,354 --> 00:09:45,268
And in Al-Hakim(ألحاكم), Imraan Bin Haseen(عمرا ن بن حصين) says that Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

121
00:09:45,514 --> 00:09:51,336
مَقَامُ الرَّجُلِ فِي الصَّفِّ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَفْضَلُ مِنْ عِبَادَةِ رَجُلٍ سِتِّينَ سَنَةً

122
00:09:51,686 --> 00:09:56,189
Standing in the ranks before the battle starts, standing, just standing in the ranks,

123
00:09:56,721 --> 00:10:01,816
Rasool Allah ﷺ says is better than worshiping Allah for 60 years.

124
00:10:02,165 --> 00:10:06,213
All of these Ahadith(احاديث) were to prepare the people spiritually for what's coming.

125
00:10:06,535 --> 00:10:09,476
They're facing enemies from every direction.

126
00:10:09,746 --> 00:10:15,570
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was telling them about the virtues of fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله عَزّوجَلّ).

127
00:10:16,423 --> 00:10:21,517
Then you had the physical preparation, and that is military training.

128
00:10:21,929 --> 00:10:27,403
Now the Sahabah didn't need to be told to go jogging or go and lift weights

129
00:10:28,047 --> 00:10:31,816
their lifestyle was active anyway, so there was no need to tell them to be physically fit.

130
00:10:32,125 --> 00:10:36,698
They had an active lifestyle because of the type of work that they would do.

131
00:10:36,867 --> 00:10:41,698
I mean a farmer going out in the farm and working from after Fajar(فجر), until late in the day,

132
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:44,484
wouldn't make sense to tell him to go jogging after that.

133
00:10:45,615 --> 00:10:49,111
So, they were physically fit so they didn't need to be told to be fit.

134
00:10:49,191 --> 00:10:54,889
However, in the areas where there were deficiencies, Rasool Allah ﷺ did specify.

135
00:10:55,595 --> 00:11:01,987
For example swimming because the Arabs of Makkah and Madina were far away from the sea

136
00:11:02,879 --> 00:11:08,312
and they are living in the desert, swimming wasn't part of their life.

137
00:11:08,392 --> 00:11:11,800
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told them in some Ahadith(أحاديث) to swim.

138
00:11:12,419 --> 00:11:21,166
So, the areas where there was deficiency, Rasool Allah ﷺ did mentioned in a Ahadith(احاديث) ways to improve them, in those areas.

139
00:11:22,016 --> 00:11:26,509
But Rasool Allah ﷺ told them for examples to train, in terms of target shooting, marksmanship.

140
00:11:27,133 --> 00:11:28,585
In his Tafseer(تفسير) of the Ayah(آية)

141
00:11:28,625 --> 00:11:30,132
 وَأَعِدُّوا لَهُمْ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُمْ مِنْ قُوَّةٍ

142
00:11:30,172 --> 00:11:31,029
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

143
00:11:31,069 --> 00:11:34,775
أَلَا إِنَّ الْقُوَّة الرَّمْي، أَلَا إِنَّ الْقُوَّة الرَّمْي، أَلَا إِنَّ الْقُوَّة الرَّمْي

144
00:11:35,068 --> 00:11:38,178
Strength is marksmanship or target shooting.

145
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:40,837
And he repeated that three times.

146
00:11:41,514 --> 00:11:43,897
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in a Hadith(حديث),

147
00:11:44,108 --> 00:11:48,615
كُلُّ شَيْءٍ لَيْسَ مِنْ ذِكْرِ اللّه عزوأجل فَهُوَ لَهْوٌ اَوْ سَهُوْ

148
00:11:48,932 --> 00:11:52,979
 إِلَّا أَرْبَعَةَ خِصَالٍ مَشْيٌ الرَجُلِ بَيْنَ الْغَرَضَيْنِ ،

149
00:11:53,321 --> 00:11:58,987
وَتَأْدِيبُهُ فَرَسَهُ ، وَمُلَاعَبَتُهُ أَهْلَهُ ، وَتَعْلِيمُ السَّبَّاحَةِ

150
00:11:59,202 --> 00:12:09,118
Rasool Allah ﷺ says everything that is not remembrance of Allahعَزّوجَلّ is a waste of your time, except four things

151
00:12:09,484 --> 00:12:10,973
walking between the targets,

152
00:12:11,473 --> 00:12:15,124
when they used to practice target shooting, it was archery,

153
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:18,928
so they would actually place two targets.

154
00:12:20,186 --> 00:12:23,435
They would stand next to the first one, and shoot at the second.

155
00:12:23,737 --> 00:12:29,394
And then they would walk to the second and pick up their arrows and then stand next to it and shoot at the first one.

156
00:12:29,609 --> 00:12:35,571
 So, this walking between the two targets, Rasool Allah ﷺ says that, that is Ibadah(عبادة) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

157
00:12:35,872 --> 00:12:38,391
Number two, training your horse.

158
00:12:38,579 --> 00:12:41,048
Number three, playing with your wife.

159
00:12:41,350 --> 00:12:45,795
Number four, learning how to swim and teaching it to others.

160
00:12:46,342 --> 00:12:50,323
 So, these four things are Ibadah(عبادة) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

161
00:12:50,542 --> 00:12:54,502
and any other form of entertainment is a waste of your time.

162
00:12:55,355 --> 00:13:01,751
So from these teachings, we can notice that there was, what is referred to as absolute war,

163
00:13:01,791 --> 00:13:06,618
 where there is a total mobilization of the society, gearing all of its resources

164
00:13:06,878 --> 00:13:12,127
towards the militarization of the society, in order to defend it.

165
00:13:12,475 --> 00:13:15,324
That process was happening in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

166
00:13:15,567 --> 00:13:17,157
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث);

167
00:13:17,268 --> 00:13:21,142
جَاهِدُوْا الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ بِأَمْوَالِكُمْ وَأَنْفُسِكُمْ وَأَلْسِنَتِكُمْ

168
00:13:21,213 --> 00:13:24,381
Fight the non believers with your wealth, arms and tongues.

169
00:13:24,452 --> 00:13:34,775
So, it was a total effort wealth, arms and tongues all geared up to defend the newly formed Muslim community.

170
00:13:35,686 --> 00:13:45,499
I hope these points would clear some misconceptions or misunderstandings regarding what was happening in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

171
00:13:45,769 --> 00:13:48,864
 we need to look at it in the context of this situation.

172
00:13:49,222 --> 00:13:54,549
It was a very difficult time for the Muslims, Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) was threatening them.

173
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:58,952
For example, as soon as Rasool Allah ﷺ made Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina,

174
00:13:59,317 --> 00:14:03,313
the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) sent a letter to Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن ابي) telling him

175
00:14:03,498 --> 00:14:06,923
that you have given sanctuary to As-Subah(ألصباء),

176
00:14:07,217 --> 00:14:12,090
You have given sanctuary to these people, they would use this derogatory term As-Subah(ألصباء).

177
00:14:12,409 --> 00:14:18,969
And you either give them up and hand them over Otherwise, we're going to kill you

178
00:14:19,315 --> 00:14:24,533
and leave your women as widows and leave your children as orphans.

179
00:14:25,226 --> 00:14:27,031
So, they were threatening the people of Madina.

180
00:14:27,246 --> 00:14:32,787
It's not like Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were turning a blind eye to the Sahabahرضي الله عنهم,

181
00:14:32,827 --> 00:14:36,128
they were taking this Hijrah(هجرة) issue very seriously, so the threat was there.

182
00:14:36,342 --> 00:14:41,609
Another example is when Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعدبن معاذ) went to visit Makkah

183
00:14:42,374 --> 00:14:45,253
He was friends with Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(امية بن خلف).

184
00:14:45,650 --> 00:14:50,107
So he went to Ummayyah(امية)and said O Ummayyah(امية), I want to make Tawaf(طواف) around the Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

185
00:14:50,409 --> 00:14:54,763
 So, tell me about a time when it would be empty, there would be crowds of people.

186
00:14:55,187 --> 00:15:00,925
So, they waited until a late hour and then they went to go and make Tawaf(طواف).

187
00:15:01,203 --> 00:15:05,231
So, Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(امية بن خلف) and Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعدبن معاذ) were friends in Jahiliya(جاهليه),

188
00:15:05,604 --> 00:15:08,238
they were making Tawaf(طواف) and then Abu Jahal(ابو جهل) saw them.

189
00:15:09,056 --> 00:15:11,754
So, Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) came to them and said, and told Ummayyah(امية);

190
00:15:11,873 --> 00:15:13,262
Who is this man with you?

191
00:15:13,514 --> 00:15:15,429
So, Ummayyah(امية) said This is Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعدبن معاذ)

192
00:15:15,660 --> 00:15:21,972
and Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعدبن معاذ) was well known, he was the head of Al-Aos(الاوس) one of the two tribes in Madina, who became Muslim.

193
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:24,656
So, Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) told Ummayyah(امية).

194
00:15:25,157 --> 00:15:30,712
I don't want to see you having this man, make Tawaf(طواف) around the Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

195
00:15:30,752 --> 00:15:34,567
 when they have given sanctuary to Muhammad(محمد) and his followers.

196
00:15:36,378 --> 00:15:39,041
So, Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعدبن معاذ) responded back by saying;

197
00:15:39,081 --> 00:15:43,471
if you prevent me from making Tawaf(طواف), I'm going to prevent your caravans from reaching to Ash-sham(الشام).

198
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:46,200
Because the caravans of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), passed next to Madina,

199
00:15:47,001 --> 00:15:48,538
so they exchanged threats.

200
00:15:49,058 --> 00:15:55,461
But this shows you that the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were plotting against Muhammadﷺ and the Sahabah.

201
00:15:55,699 --> 00:16:04,361
And that's why there was a militarization effort going on in Madina, it was to protect the Muslim community.

202
00:16:07,879 --> 00:16:15,022
Rasool Allah ﷺ, after receiving permission from Allahعَزّوجَلّ to fight.

203
00:16:15,483 --> 00:16:19,231
 أُذِنَ لِلَّذِينَ يُقَاتَلُونَ بِأَنَّهُمْ ظُلِمُوا ۚ

204
00:16:20,429 --> 00:16:26,054
Rasool Allah ﷺ started sending out what is referred to as Sarayya(سرايه).

205
00:16:27,370 --> 00:16:31,465
So, you have in our books of Seerah(سيرة) Saraya(سرايا), and you have Gazawaat(غزوات).

206
00:16:32,396 --> 00:16:34,107
So, what's the difference between the two?

207
00:16:34,936 --> 00:16:38,900
So you would have Ghazwat Badr(غزوة البدر) and you'd have Ghazwat Uhud(غزوة احد),

208
00:16:39,417 --> 00:16:41,032
and you'd have Ghazwat Khandaq(غزوة الخندق).

209
00:16:41,819 --> 00:16:48,363
On the other hand, you would have, Sariyat Abu Obaidah(سرية ابو عبيده), Sariyat Abdullah Bin Jahash(سرية عبدالله بن جحش),

210
00:16:48,702 --> 00:16:51,447
Sariyat Sa'ad Ibn Abi Waqas(سرية سعد إبن أبي وقاص).

211
00:16:52,579 --> 00:17:00,508
The difference is Saraya(سرايا) referred to the armies that were sent out by Rasool Allah ﷺ without him participating in them.

212
00:17:01,574 --> 00:17:07,632
While a Ghazwa(غزوة) is an army that is led by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

213
00:17:08,114 --> 00:17:11,389
So, that's the difference between a Ghazwa(غزوه) and a Sariyah(سريه).

214
00:17:11,894 --> 00:17:16,613
 If you're reading a book of Seerah(سيرة), you'll run into this, Sariyah(سريه) and Ghazwa(غزوة).

215
00:17:18,142 --> 00:17:22,740
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ started sending out Sarayah(سرايه), and he was leading Ghazawaat(غزوات).

216
00:17:22,805 --> 00:17:29,598
Now in terms of the linguistic meaning of the two words, Ghazwa(غزوة) and Sariyah(سريه).

217
00:17:29,638 --> 00:17:32,938
Ghazwa(غزوة) means, an army of conquest.

218
00:17:33,946 --> 00:17:36,472
That's the linguistic meaning of Ghazwa(غزوه).

219
00:17:37,201 --> 00:17:43,164
While Sariyah(سريه) is an army but it doesn't really mean that it's involved in conquest or not.

220
00:17:43,969 --> 00:17:47,782
But these are just the linguistic meanings of the word that aren't really relevant,

221
00:17:47,825 --> 00:17:52,436
when it comes to how the scholars of Seerah(سيرة), are using these two words.

222
00:17:53,728 --> 00:17:58,648
The first Ghazwa(غزوة) in which Rasool Allah ﷺ participated in is called Ghazwat-Al-Abwaa(غزوة الأبوآء),

223
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:00,726
but no fighting occurred.

224
00:18:01,837 --> 00:18:04,130
 This army went out but didn't meet the enemy.

225
00:18:05,993 --> 00:18:11,280
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ sends out a Sariyyah(سريه) led by Obaidah Ibn Haris(عبيدة بن حارث),

226
00:18:11,745 --> 00:18:16,590
these were 60 of Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون), all of them were Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون), on foot.

227
00:18:17,664 --> 00:18:23,503
There were no mounts and they would walk at night and hide during the day.

228
00:18:24,871 --> 00:18:28,555
They exchanged arrows but no one was killed.

229
00:18:29,464 --> 00:18:36,062
So, the first shots fired in Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) were in Sariyat-Obaidah Bin Haris(سرية عبيده بن حارث),

230
00:18:36,718 --> 00:18:42,050
and the first one to shoot was Sa'ad Ibn Abi Waqasرضي الله عنه.

231
00:18:42,428 --> 00:18:47,316
He said: I'm the first one to strike an arrow in the path of Allah,

232
00:18:48,230 --> 00:18:50,977
I am the first one to shoot an arrow in the path of Allah.

233
00:18:51,853 --> 00:18:54,127
Then you have Sariyat-Hamza Bin Abdul Muttalib(سرية حمزه بن عبدالمطلب)

234
00:18:54,220 --> 00:18:58,554
this was Sariyah(سرية) led by Hamza Bin Abdul Muttalib(حمزه بن عبدالمطلب), about 30 Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون),

235
00:18:58,619 --> 00:19:07,798
but this time they were riding camels, and they met with a caravan.

236
00:19:07,972 --> 00:19:13,020
This was a Sariyah(سرية) that went out to raid a caravan that was belonging to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

237
00:19:13,807 --> 00:19:19,439
But the caravan was supported by a large number of guards.

238
00:19:20,219 --> 00:19:22,804
Anyway, no fighting occurred

239
00:19:22,844 --> 00:19:30,012
because one of the tribesmen in the area, who had a peace agreement with Muhammadﷺ and with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) interfered

240
00:19:30,452 --> 00:19:32,891
when he saw that and no fighting occurred.

241
00:19:34,384 --> 00:19:39,531
But when this happened, Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) was with the caravan he went back to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and he said

242
00:19:39,949 --> 00:19:42,063
he was giving warning to his people, he said;

243
00:19:42,332 --> 00:19:44,438
Muhammad(محمد) is out there to get you, be careful.

244
00:19:46,442 --> 00:19:49,586
And he was telling his people that he's like an angry lion,

245
00:19:50,603 --> 00:19:56,394
and he said because we have driven them out of the land like insects would be driven off, the back of a camel.

246
00:19:57,127 --> 00:20:01,462
So, he's telling his people to be careful Muhammadﷺ is out there

247
00:20:01,795 --> 00:20:07,391
and he's trying to lay his hands on our caravans and on us, so Be careful.

248
00:20:09,597 --> 00:20:11,988
And then there was another Ghazwa(غزوه) called Ghazwat-Bu'aat(غزوة بواط)

249
00:20:13,686 --> 00:20:16,863
They went to raid a caravan but couldn't find it.

250
00:20:17,383 --> 00:20:19,140
And then you have Ghazwat Al-Asheerah(غزوة ألعشيره).

251
00:20:19,464 --> 00:20:24,623
They also went to pursue a caravan but weren't able to find it.

252
00:20:24,998 --> 00:20:30,035
These caravans were a bit elusive, they were trying to hide their tracks in the desert.

253
00:20:31,391 --> 00:20:35,333
And then you have Sariyat Sa'ad Ibn Abi Waqas(سرية سعد إبن أبي وقاص) and Ghazwat Badr Al-Uola(غزوة البدر ألأولى),

254
00:20:35,373 --> 00:20:39,365
all of these occurred within the first two years of Hijrah(هجرة) before the Battle of Badr(بدر).

255
00:20:40,899 --> 00:20:42,971
Then there's another Sariyah(سرية) that happened

256
00:20:43,011 --> 00:20:47,493
and this Sariyah(سرية) is quite important because of the consequences of it.

257
00:20:48,230 --> 00:20:54,103
And this Sariyah(سرية) is called Sariyah(سرية) of Abdullah Bin Jahashرضي الله عنه.

258
00:20:55,909 --> 00:21:01,065
This was a small group of Sahabah رضي الله عنهم,

259
00:21:02,265 --> 00:21:07,408
who were sent out to pursue a caravan belonging to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

260
00:21:08,422 --> 00:21:14,764
Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش), the leader of this Sariyah(سرية) was handed a letter by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

261
00:21:15,966 --> 00:21:21,703
That letter was sealed and Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش), not to open it, until after two days.

262
00:21:22,644 --> 00:21:26,512
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him to go to such and such place.

263
00:21:27,067 --> 00:21:30,587
And after two days you open this letter and he read it.

264
00:21:31,690 --> 00:21:36,215
Abdullah Bin Jahashرضي الله عنه opens the letter after two days and it states in there,

265
00:21:36,453 --> 00:21:42,713
that I instruct you to go to such and such place and this place was between Makkah and At-Taef(ألطائف)

266
00:21:43,710 --> 00:21:49,385
and to ask the members of your Sariyah(سرية) to follow you,

267
00:21:50,269 --> 00:21:52,043
but make it volunteer on them.

268
00:21:52,909 --> 00:21:56,112
So, this was a voluntary Sariyah(سرية).

269
00:21:56,726 --> 00:21:59,136
You asked them if they want to join you or not.

270
00:22:00,092 --> 00:22:03,187
Probably the reason was because this was quite a risky operation.

271
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:11,206
These men were going deep in the territory of Al-Kuffar(الكفار), they were going between Makkah and At-Taef(ألطائف).

272
00:22:11,956 --> 00:22:16,154
So now, Rasool Allah ﷺ wasn't raiding a caravan that was passing next to Madina,

273
00:22:16,194 --> 00:22:22,577
you know, because the route that leads from Makkah to Syria passes next to Madina.

274
00:22:22,959 --> 00:22:27,260
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ had the opportunity of intersecting those caravans.

275
00:22:27,710 --> 00:22:35,053
Now Rasool Allah ﷺ was going after the caravans of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), which were between Makkah and At-Taef(ألطائف).

276
00:22:36,313 --> 00:22:43,671
So, this was quite risky and they would be quite far away from their base, Al-Madina.

277
00:22:44,673 --> 00:22:49,492
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ makes this voluntary Sariyah(سرية).

278
00:22:51,325 --> 00:22:53,041
Abdullah Bin Jabir(Jahash)رضي الله عنه

279
00:22:54,025 --> 00:22:58,883
tells the member of his Sariyah(سرية), this is what Rasool Allah ﷺ says, I'm going to go.

280
00:22:59,467 --> 00:23:02,598
And whoever wants to follow me, it's up to you.

281
00:23:03,162 --> 00:23:07,183
So it was voluntary, on all of them, including Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش).

282
00:23:08,135 --> 00:23:10,581
 They all said, we're willing to go with you, we're going to go.

283
00:23:12,077 --> 00:23:16,279
Because Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) told them, whoever wants to stay can stay, and whoever wants to go and die,

284
00:23:16,490 --> 00:23:20,288
you're welcome to come, they saw it as quite a risky operation.

285
00:23:21,100 --> 00:23:25,048
They said we're all willing to die Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), we're going to go with you.

286
00:23:25,322 --> 00:23:27,371
So none of them stayed behind.

287
00:23:28,036 --> 00:23:33,830
You can contrast this with all of the news of soldiers defecting from their armies.

288
00:23:34,219 --> 00:23:38,546
So you can see how some people are forced to fight.

289
00:23:38,973 --> 00:23:42,081
While, some people volunteer for it.

290
00:23:42,384 --> 00:23:49,848
And this shows you the difference between when somebody is doing something for the sake of this world for greed,

291
00:23:50,559 --> 00:23:55,810
or for expansion of territory, or for power,

292
00:23:56,458 --> 00:24:00,805
compared to when somebody is doing something virtuous for the sake of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

293
00:24:01,073 --> 00:24:06,271
And this again, shows you the difference between fighting for the sake of Allah and fighting for other reasons,

294
00:24:06,351 --> 00:24:13,192
 which we talked about in our previous session, that all war is evil, except if it is fought for the sake of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

295
00:24:14,245 --> 00:24:17,584
So here they all volunteered to go.

296
00:24:19,019 --> 00:24:22,540
 They do a spot the caravan of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

297
00:24:23,081 --> 00:24:26,519
the caravan was lightly guarded only four guards.

298
00:24:27,320 --> 00:24:32,645
And they were within striking distance, but they were in a dilemma.

299
00:24:33,412 --> 00:24:34,886
This was the sacred month,

300
00:24:35,903 --> 00:24:40,304
there were four months in the year in which Arabs do not fight.

301
00:24:41,010 --> 00:24:46,058
And this was agreed upon, among them and they held this up in high esteem,

302
00:24:46,379 --> 00:24:52,906
they took these months seriously, they wouldn't violate them and they wouldn't fight in them.

303
00:24:54,306 --> 00:25:01,223
They were in the last day of the month of Rajab(رجب), which is one of the sacred months.

304
00:25:01,991 --> 00:25:03,565
So, they're not supposed to fight.

305
00:25:04,907 --> 00:25:06,236
So, you might ask the question.?

306
00:25:06,276 --> 00:25:08,377
Well, why not just wait for another day

307
00:25:08,810 --> 00:25:14,897
pursue this caravan and just have one more day to go and then you'll be in the month of Shaban(شعبان), you can attack them.

308
00:25:15,289 --> 00:25:16,716
Well, there is another problem.

309
00:25:16,752 --> 00:25:23,386
If they wait for another day, this caravan would enter into the sacred limits of Makkah

310
00:25:23,914 --> 00:25:25,769
where they're not supposed to fight either.

311
00:25:26,094 --> 00:25:34,415
So either way, they will be violating either the sanctity of the four months, or the sanctity of Makkah.

312
00:25:35,576 --> 00:25:37,173
So it was a dilemma, they made Shuraa(شورى).

313
00:25:37,685 --> 00:25:42,406
And they decided to go ahead and attack in the month of Rajab(رجب) in the sacred month.

314
00:25:43,759 --> 00:25:49,206
They shot their arrows, one of the four guards was killed, Al-Hazrami(ألحضرمي).

315
00:25:50,079 --> 00:25:57,276
One of them ran away, and Two of them were taken prisoners and the whole caravan fell into the hands of the Muslims.

316
00:25:58,136 --> 00:26:02,804
So, they drove them back to Madina, this was breaking news.

317
00:26:03,257 --> 00:26:06,741
Everyone was talking about it, Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) made a big deal about it.

318
00:26:07,275 --> 00:26:11,155
They took this opportunity and milked it, to the limits.

319
00:26:11,705 --> 00:26:17,490
They went around saying that Muhammad(محمد) and his people are violating the sacred months,

320
00:26:17,778 --> 00:26:26,073
they are shedding blood, they have taken prisoners, they have stealed our wealth, all in the holy months.

321
00:26:26,898 --> 00:26:27,701
It says in Al-Bayhaqi(البيهقي);

322
00:26:27,741 --> 00:26:31,481
 قَدِ اسْتَحلَّ محمد وَاَصْحَابُه’ شَهْرَالْحَرَامْ

323
00:26:31,806 --> 00:26:36,526
وَسَفَكُوْا فِيْهِ الدَّمْ وَاَخَذُوْا فِيْهِ الْاَمْوَالْ وَاَسَرُوْا فِيْهِ الرِّجَالْ

324
00:26:37,459 --> 00:26:43,734
Muhammad(محمد) and his people have violated the sacred months, and they have shed blood

325
00:26:43,998 --> 00:26:48,950
and they have taken our wealth, and they have taken our men prisoners.

326
00:26:50,013 --> 00:26:56,274
So again, this was breaking news on all networks splashing the front pages of every newspaper in the country.

327
00:26:56,959 --> 00:27:03,994
The Muslims are terrorists, who are violating the sanctity of the holy month,

328
00:27:04,579 --> 00:27:08,503
shedding blood and they went around, spreading this news in Arabia.

329
00:27:09,168 --> 00:27:10,487
And it was a big deal.

330
00:27:12,183 --> 00:27:15,083
Well, when the men of the Sariyah(سرية) came back to Madina.

331
00:27:15,123 --> 00:27:18,048
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them, I didn't tell you to fight in the holy month,

332
00:27:18,964 --> 00:27:20,876
I didn't give you those instructions.

333
00:27:21,477 --> 00:27:26,220
And the Muslims were reproaching the Sahabah, Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) and his people,

334
00:27:26,260 --> 00:27:28,891
they were telling them; Who told you to fight in the sacred month.?

335
00:27:29,519 --> 00:27:30,674
Who told you to violate it?

336
00:27:31,292 --> 00:27:36,121
So, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) these men of the Sariyah(سرية) were in a very difficult situation

337
00:27:36,727 --> 00:27:40,536
they were worried, they were very worried. What have we done.

338
00:27:40,895 --> 00:27:44,504
And What will this be considered in the eyes of Allahعَزّوجَلّ?

339
00:27:44,965 --> 00:27:50,734
And Rasool Allah ﷺ refused to take the prisoners and he refused to take the caravan.

340
00:27:51,316 --> 00:27:54,724
So, you can imagine how desperate these Sahabah would be.

341
00:27:54,764 --> 00:28:00,541
I mean, we went out there, we risked our lives and then here we are all what we have done is not accepted.

342
00:28:01,089 --> 00:28:04,639
And everybody's upset with us, Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah alike

343
00:28:05,759 --> 00:28:10,539
and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) they were taking advantage of this, and they made a big deal out of it.

344
00:28:11,374 --> 00:28:13,737
And then Ayyat(آيات) from Qur'an were revealed,

345
00:28:14,270 --> 00:28:16,945
Verse to 217 from Surat-Ul-Bakara(سورة البقره).

346
00:28:17,386 --> 00:28:23,651
يَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الشَّهْرِ الْحَرَامِ قِتَالٍ فِيهِ ۖ

347
00:28:23,969 --> 00:28:27,855
They ask you about the sacred month, about fighting therein.

348
00:28:28,569 --> 00:28:34,938
So now, people are asking, what is the ruling of Allahعَزّوجَلّ concerning fighting in the sacred month.

349
00:28:36,231 --> 00:28:37,586
 So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says,

350
00:28:37,817 --> 00:28:41,790
قُلْ قِتَالٌ فِيهِ كَبِيرٌ ۖ

351
00:28:42,257 --> 00:28:44,835
Say fighting therein is a great sin,

352
00:28:45,109 --> 00:28:50,496
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), so what Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) and his men did was a great sin.

353
00:28:50,941 --> 00:28:56,562
Allahعَزّوجَلّ was saying, that fighting in the sacred month is a great sin.

354
00:28:58,157 --> 00:28:59,961
But then what did Allahعَزّوجَلّ say,

355
00:29:00,821 --> 00:29:08,848
وَصَدٌّ عَنْ سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَكُفْرٌ بِهِ وَالْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ

356
00:29:09,252 --> 00:29:16,739
 وَالْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَام وَإِخْرَاجُ أَهْلِهِ مِنْهُ أَكْبَرُ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ ۚ

357
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:21,010
وَالْفِتْنَةُ أَكْبَرُ مِنَ الْقَتْلِ ۗ

358
00:29:21,221 --> 00:29:23,864
So, here Allahعَزّوجَلّ is putting things in perspective.

359
00:29:24,203 --> 00:29:26,058
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is saying that yes,

360
00:29:26,482 --> 00:29:31,089
what the Sahabah have done in violating the sanctity of the sacred month

361
00:29:31,168 --> 00:29:33,146
It was wrong, it was a great sin,

362
00:29:33,470 --> 00:29:36,991
but then Allahعَزّوجَلّ lists four other sins.

363
00:29:37,193 --> 00:29:41,362
Number one, averting the people away from the path of Allah.

364
00:29:41,528 --> 00:29:46,491
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), on the other hand were averting people from the path of Allah,

365
00:29:46,538 --> 00:29:49,384
they were standing between people and becoming Muslim.

366
00:29:49,689 --> 00:29:52,075
They were standing between them and becoming Muslim.

367
00:29:52,357 --> 00:29:56,452
 Number two, and disbelief in him, that is a great sin.

368
00:29:56,900 --> 00:30:00,651
Number three, and preventing access to Al-Masjid-Al-Haraam(مسجد الحرام).

369
00:30:00,806 --> 00:30:03,858
The Muslims were not allowed to go to Makkah,

370
00:30:04,497 --> 00:30:10,472
Number four, and the expulsion of its people there from and the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) were driven out of Makkah.

371
00:30:10,616 --> 00:30:16,315
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says; Those sins are greater than what's Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) did.

372
00:30:16,935 --> 00:30:22,893
So, averting people from the way of Allah is a greater sin, then killing in the sacred month.

373
00:30:23,286 --> 00:30:27,936
Disbelieving in Allah is a greater sin than killing in the sacred month.

374
00:30:28,261 --> 00:30:34,946
And preventing access to Al-Masjid-Al-Haraam(مسجد الحرام) is a greater evil in the eyes of Allah, than fighting the sacred month

375
00:30:35,264 --> 00:30:37,764
and the expulsion of people from Makkah

376
00:30:38,024 --> 00:30:44,681
and forcing them out of their land is a greater sin in the eyes of Allah, than fighting in the sacred month.

377
00:30:44,895 --> 00:30:47,183
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is putting things in perspective.

378
00:30:48,658 --> 00:30:50,001
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

379
00:30:50,239 --> 00:30:53,096
وَالْفِتْنَةُ أَكْبَرُ مِنَ الْقَتْلِ ۗ

380
00:30:53,469 --> 00:31:00,140
And fitna(فتنه) seducing people away from Islam is greater than killing.

381
00:31:01,222 --> 00:31:02,516
Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) says;

382
00:31:02,708 --> 00:31:06,966
كَانُوْ يَفْتِنُوْنَ الْمُسْلِمَه فِيْ دِيْنِهِ حَتَّى يَرُدُّه’ اِلَى الْكُفْرْ

383
00:31:07,249 --> 00:31:11,648
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) will seduce a Muslim, until he gives up Islam.

384
00:31:11,937 --> 00:31:15,451
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says, that is worse than fighting in the sacred month.

385
00:31:17,003 --> 00:31:20,126
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ says about disbelievers.

386
00:31:20,473 --> 00:31:29,152
وَلَا يَزَالُونَ يُقَاتِلُونَكُمْ حَتَّىٰ يَرُدُّوكُمْ عَنْ دِينِكُمْ إِنِ اسْتَطَاعُوا ۚ

387
00:31:29,721 --> 00:31:38,283
وَمَنْ يَرْتَدِدْ مِنْكُمْ عَنْ دِينِهِ فَيَمُتْ وَهُوَ كَافِرٌ فَأُولَٰئِكَ

388
00:31:38,788 --> 00:31:45,125
فَأُولَٰئِكَ حَبِطَتْ أَعْمَالُهُمْ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ ۖ

389
00:31:45,518 --> 00:31:52,347
وَأُولَٰئِكَ أَصْحَابُ النَّارِ ۖ هُمْ فِيهَا خَالِدُونَ۝

390
00:31:53,029 --> 00:31:58,540
This Ayah(آية) is clearing up the minds of people, it's telling them;

391
00:31:59,009 --> 00:32:02,725
 Look at what Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) and his people did.

392
00:32:03,080 --> 00:32:07,986
And look at, on the other hand, what the Kuffar(كفار) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) have been doing for 13 years,

393
00:32:08,707 --> 00:32:11,336
don't just make a big deal about what Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) did

394
00:32:11,376 --> 00:32:14,763
and completely forget about the sins of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

395
00:32:15,034 --> 00:32:17,778
even though what Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) did was wrong.

396
00:32:18,182 --> 00:32:23,956
But what the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) have been doing, outweighs all of that.

397
00:32:24,698 --> 00:32:28,610
So, when these Ayaat(آيات) were revealed, Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) and his followers were happy,

398
00:32:28,690 --> 00:32:35,717
at least that Allahعَزّوجَلّ has mentioned that the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) have committed greater sins.

399
00:32:35,984 --> 00:32:39,642
So now, they were eager to get credit for what they have done.

400
00:32:39,829 --> 00:32:45,136
So now, if these Ayaat(آيات) make them break even, or at least that's how it appears now.

401
00:32:45,176 --> 00:32:48,895
They went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and they wanted to get reward for what they have done.

402
00:32:49,163 --> 00:32:53,101
Even though the Ayah(آية) says that it was a mistake, it was a sin.

403
00:32:54,032 --> 00:32:58,706
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ reveals the following Ayah(آية), which was Ayah(آية ) Verse 218.

404
00:32:59,153 --> 00:33:00,466
Allahعَزّوجَلّ said;

405
00:33:01,285 --> 00:33:13,981
إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَالَّذِينَ هَاجَرُوا وَجَاهَدُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أُولَٰئِكَ يَرْجُونَ رَحْمَتَ اللَّهِ ۚ

406
00:33:15,139 --> 00:33:18,818
وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ۝

407
00:33:19,309 --> 00:33:25,124
Indeed, those who have believed and those who have immigrated and fought in the cause of Allah,

408
00:33:25,417 --> 00:33:29,862
those expect the mercy of Allah, and Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.

409
00:33:30,035 --> 00:33:30,665
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله).

410
00:33:30,836 --> 00:33:37,199
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling them that you can expect the mercy of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, and expect to get credit for what you have done

411
00:33:37,407 --> 00:33:40,158
and expect to be given the reward of the Mujahideen(مجاهدين).

412
00:33:41,680 --> 00:33:48,234
Not only that, Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) and his Sariyyah(سريه) according to our scholars,

413
00:33:48,595 --> 00:33:52,988
they were the first to take prisoners and the path of Allah.

414
00:33:53,348 --> 00:33:57,217
They were the first to take booty of war in the path of Allah,

415
00:33:57,549 --> 00:34:01,077
and they were the first to kill a disbeliever in the path of Allah.

416
00:34:01,337 --> 00:34:07,278
So, they were the first in these three areas and that was an honor, that was bestowed on them.

417
00:34:08,670 --> 00:34:16,832
When these Ayaat(آيات) were revealed, Rasool Allah ﷺ took the caravan, and he took the two men as prisoners.

418
00:34:17,828 --> 00:34:21,618
 So, the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) came to ransom them, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

419
00:34:21,996 --> 00:34:26,149
اَخَافُ اَنْ تَكُوْنُوْا قَدْ عَصَبْتُمْ سَعْد اِبْنِ مَالك وَ عُتْبَه بِنْ غَزْوَانْ

420
00:34:26,708 --> 00:34:32,517
Two of the members of the Sariyyah(سريه) of Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) lost the camel, so they went looking for it.

421
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:35,151
And they didn't come back yet.

422
00:34:35,829 --> 00:34:38,128
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told that people have Quraish(قُرَيْشْ);

423
00:34:38,391 --> 00:34:45,080
 I'm not going to hand over, until my two men come back, I fear that you might kill them.

424
00:34:45,420 --> 00:34:49,532
So, this shows you the care that Rasool Allah ﷺ had for his followers.

425
00:34:49,781 --> 00:34:52,944
He said, I'm not giving you your two men, until my two men come back.

426
00:34:54,201 --> 00:34:56,958
And this is how the Muslims should be.

427
00:34:57,082 --> 00:34:59,326
They should never give one another up.

428
00:35:00,350 --> 00:35:04,850
So, when Sa'ad Ibn Malik(سَعْد اِبْنِ مَالك) and Utba Bin Ghazwaan(عُتْبَه بِنْ غَزْوَانْ) came back,

429
00:35:05,189 --> 00:35:10,465
Rasool Allah ﷺ released the two prisoners of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they were ransomed.

430
00:35:10,638 --> 00:35:12,886
 The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) had to pay money to free them

431
00:35:13,442 --> 00:35:18,113
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), one of them Al-Hakam Bin Kaisaan(ألحكم بن كيسان) became Muslim, and he stayed, he didn't go back.

432
00:35:19,791 --> 00:35:21,913
And he died as a Shaheed(شهيد) later on.

433
00:35:22,087 --> 00:35:27,476
While the other Uthman Bin Mugheera(عثمان بن مغيرة), he went back to Makkah, and died as a disbelievers.

434
00:35:28,126 --> 00:35:30,297
So, some lessons from this Sariyyah(سريه).

435
00:35:30,665 --> 00:35:36,892
Number one, the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ are gonna pick on your actions,

436
00:35:37,718 --> 00:35:40,451
and they're going to try to blow them out of proportion,

437
00:35:40,848 --> 00:35:51,171
they might try to twist the truth and they will try to present you in the worst form they are capable of presenting you in.

438
00:35:51,611 --> 00:35:58,059
So, the Muslim needs to be aware of that, and needs to study the reality of the situation and put things in perspective,

439
00:35:58,415 --> 00:36:01,573
just like these Ayaat(آيات) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, put things in perspective.

440
00:36:02,093 --> 00:36:09,164
So, if Muslims are ever accused of being terrorists, or that Islam is promoting violence.

441
00:36:09,884 --> 00:36:17,072
Let whoever is saying that, remember that Hundreds of thousands of people were killed in Iraq,

442
00:36:17,996 --> 00:36:22,143
that Palestinians have been suffering for over 50 years

443
00:36:22,719 --> 00:36:29,929
that Muslims in Kashmir and Chechnya and the Philippines and one can go on and on and on have been suffering for a very long time.

444
00:36:31,073 --> 00:36:32,536
Bring these things up.

445
00:36:32,840 --> 00:36:39,767
And it will become clear that even if the Muslims, do something that is not justified

446
00:36:39,847 --> 00:36:43,400
that cannot fall under justifiable resistance

447
00:36:44,129 --> 00:36:52,379
it can never reach to the level of violence and evil that is committed against the Muslims, from the disbelievers.

448
00:36:52,991 --> 00:36:54,516
It can never reach to that level.

449
00:36:55,388 --> 00:37:03,832
I mean, more than a million have been killed in the sanctions that were laid upon Iraq, more than a million.

450
00:37:04,982 --> 00:37:08,175
So, things need to be put in the right perspective,

451
00:37:08,543 --> 00:37:15,092
and don't be gullible and naive and just fall into what the media is saying, because the media is not on your side.

452
00:37:16,525 --> 00:37:19,167
And the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ are never going to be on your side.

453
00:37:20,055 --> 00:37:23,602
So, the Muslim needs to be aware about the reality of the situation,

454
00:37:23,818 --> 00:37:30,281
and not just take things as you hear it, on the radio or TV, but look deep into what is happening.

455
00:37:30,555 --> 00:37:34,379
And you'll see the evil that is caused by the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

456
00:37:34,869 --> 00:37:41,618
 Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) Look at how what Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) did to Muhammadﷺ, the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ are doing to the Muslims today.

457
00:37:42,589 --> 00:37:51,474
The preachers who are preaching the true Islam are being thrown in jail or killed or subjugated to threats.

458
00:37:52,381 --> 00:37:58,996
If Muslims try to present the truth, as it is, they are fought against and they are restricted.

459
00:37:59,302 --> 00:38:05,700
Muslim lands are taken as booty and milking cows for the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

460
00:38:05,993 --> 00:38:08,600
Muslim blood has become very cheap.

461
00:38:09,408 --> 00:38:12,272
In fact, it has not only become cheap, it has become worthless.

462
00:38:14,317 --> 00:38:17,564
Number two, second lesson

463
00:38:18,119 --> 00:38:21,468
the care that Muslims should have for one another.

464
00:38:21,872 --> 00:38:30,570
Rasool Allah ﷺ refused to give up the two prisoners of war, until Utba(عتبه) and Sa'ad Ibn Malik(سعدابن مالك) would come back.

465
00:38:31,804 --> 00:38:37,178
 And then, a few lessons regarding the issue of Saraya(سرايه) in general

466
00:38:37,728 --> 00:38:44,741
these Sarayah( سرايه) were to establish the military presence of Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Muslims.

467
00:38:45,478 --> 00:38:52,799
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was sending the Saraya(سرايا) north, south, west, east to let the people know

468
00:38:53,247 --> 00:38:58,944
that the Muslims have force and they are capable of using it and this is a strong state.

469
00:38:58,981 --> 00:39:04,551
So, be careful don't attack it, because you know the tribal system of old Arabia.

470
00:39:05,078 --> 00:39:09,003
 If one tribe feels that the other tribe is weak, they take advantage of that.

471
00:39:10,120 --> 00:39:14,803
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was sending out these Sarayah(سرايا) as a deterrence to others,

472
00:39:14,969 --> 00:39:21,116
to the Bedouins who are surrounding Madina who still have the respect of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) in their hearts,

473
00:39:21,156 --> 00:39:26,562
you know, because Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) was seen as the center of the Arabia, the noble men,

474
00:39:26,793 --> 00:39:30,999
they were the people who were the custodians of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

475
00:39:31,317 --> 00:39:34,575
So, they were held in high esteem by the rest of Arabia.

476
00:39:34,756 --> 00:39:42,226
Rasool Allah ﷺ was trying to break that and trying to let the people know that there is now rival power in the area.

477
00:39:43,308 --> 00:39:44,205
Number two,

478
00:39:44,392 --> 00:39:48,526
Rasool Allah ﷺ was winning over tribes and establishing alliances,

479
00:39:49,756 --> 00:39:55,528
and this was still in the stage, where Rasool Allah ﷺ could establish alliances with Polytheists.

480
00:39:56,031 --> 00:40:00,036
We talked about the stages of fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) that in the final stage,

481
00:40:00,076 --> 00:40:03,543
Rasool Allah ﷺ was instructed to fight all of the Mushrikeen(مشركين)

482
00:40:03,763 --> 00:40:09,434
but we're still in the stage here, where Rasool Allah ﷺ could establish alliances with these tribes

483
00:40:09,484 --> 00:40:14,183
and he did, with some of the Bedouin tribe surrounding Madina, he established alliances.

484
00:40:14,641 --> 00:40:19,550
This was done through these Saraya(سرايا), You can translate Sariyyah(سريه) as expedition.

485
00:40:20,832 --> 00:40:24,904
Number three, these Sarayah(سرايا) were mostly for economical reasons.

486
00:40:25,829 --> 00:40:31,618
These were to raid caravans, mostly these Saraya(سرايا) were sent out to raid the caravans of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

487
00:40:31,990 --> 00:40:34,478
That is because in the Islamic Fiqh(فقه),

488
00:40:34,954 --> 00:40:44,988
if the Muslim state is in war with another, is in a state of war, that makes the lives and the wealth of the enemy state Halal(حلال).

489
00:40:45,774 --> 00:40:52,151
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was attacking the economical network of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

490
00:40:52,933 --> 00:40:59,998
And this was a serious threat to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and this is what led to the Battle of Badr(ألبدر)

491
00:41:00,633 --> 00:41:07,057
because it started out as we will see as an attempt to take over the biggest caravan of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

492
00:41:07,097 --> 00:41:09,395
which was led by Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان).

493
00:41:09,737 --> 00:41:13,863
Number four, these Sarayah(سرايا) were training for the Muslims.

494
00:41:14,729 --> 00:41:22,259
Now Rasool Allah ﷺ is not fighting a tribal warfare, this is an army with a new identity.

495
00:41:22,713 --> 00:41:28,830
So, these Sarayah(سرايه) were a great chance for the Sahabah, to experience and to learn.

496
00:41:29,191 --> 00:41:32,445
He would send out groups of 30, groups of 60.

497
00:41:32,654 --> 00:41:38,366
Many of these Sarayah(سرايا), they would learn reconnaissance methods, they would learn how to ambush,

498
00:41:38,517 --> 00:41:42,291
they would learn the area, they would get to know the tribes around them.

499
00:41:42,456 --> 00:41:46,939
So, they were benefiting greatly from these Sarayah(سرايا), and overall, they were quite successful,

500
00:41:47,894 --> 00:41:53,024
in this war that carried on for a few years between Rasool Allah ﷺ and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

501
00:41:53,926 --> 00:42:00,052
you would find that Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) didn't have a similar tactic of sending out Sarayah(سرايا) against the Muslims.

502
00:42:00,613 --> 00:42:03,001
This was pretty much an Islamic thing,

503
00:42:03,403 --> 00:42:08,362
and they were very successful and they were a serious threat, to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

504
00:42:09,869 --> 00:42:14,392
Rasool Allah ﷺ wasn't totally secure in Madina

505
00:42:15,287 --> 00:42:21,831
and Madina was small and the number of Muslims wasn't that large.

506
00:42:22,286 --> 00:42:29,274
And Rasool Allah ﷺ, one night couldn't sleep, and he said, I wish there's somebody to guard me, in this night.

507
00:42:30,140 --> 00:42:35,515
And suddenly he heard the sound of someone outside carrying his weapons.

508
00:42:35,825 --> 00:42:37,910
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ asked who is it?

509
00:42:38,348 --> 00:42:42,242
And it turned out to be Sa'ad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدابن ابي وقاص), he came to guard Rasool Allah ﷺ.

510
00:42:44,089 --> 00:42:48,743
Ibn Hajar(إبن حجر) gives us some lessons from this incident.

511
00:42:49,212 --> 00:42:54,724
He says; This shows that the Muslim should not be careless, when care is needed.

512
00:42:55,965 --> 00:43:00,173
So, Rasool Allahﷺ was threatened in Madina.

513
00:43:01,104 --> 00:43:02,872
And he wasn't careless about it.

514
00:43:03,261 --> 00:43:09,255
He couldn't actually sleep that night, because he wanted someone to be his guard.

515
00:43:09,904 --> 00:43:12,336
 So, the Muslim should be careful.

516
00:43:12,791 --> 00:43:16,827
Number two, he says that, "the Muslims should protect their leaders, should guard their leaders

517
00:43:17,928 --> 00:43:21,009
should guard their Ulemaa(علماء), should guard their military leaders.

518
00:43:21,449 --> 00:43:27,824
Number three, he said, that Rasool Allah ﷺ did this as a lesson for his Ummah(امة),

519
00:43:28,076 --> 00:43:33,378
in fact that he wasn't able to sleep is, and then was asking for somebody to guard him,

520
00:43:33,418 --> 00:43:40,135
this is a lesson to his Ummah(امة) that we should be careful, we should be alert and this carried on,

521
00:43:41,101 --> 00:43:42,796
until Allahعَزّوجَلّ reveal the Ayah(آية).

522
00:43:42,836 --> 00:43:44,629
وَاللَّهُ يَعْصِمُكَ مِنَ النَّاسِ ۗ

523
00:43:45,083 --> 00:43:47,023
Allah will protect you from people.

524
00:43:47,063 --> 00:43:52,102
So, Allah was telling Muhammadﷺ you don't need to have guards, Allahعَزّوجَلّ will protect you.

525
00:43:52,488 --> 00:43:58,349
And that's when Rasool Allah ﷺ came out and said, go back, Allahعَزّوجَلّ has given me, His protection.

526
00:43:59,353 --> 00:44:00,590
They had a census,

527
00:44:01,254 --> 00:44:07,673
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Count all the souls that profess Islam.

528
00:44:08,949 --> 00:44:14,314
So, the total number of men of fighting age was 1500.

529
00:44:15,468 --> 00:44:18,044
And then the Sahabah asked the question.

530
00:44:18,456 --> 00:44:22,679
We are 1500, we shouldn't be afraid then.

531
00:44:23,581 --> 00:44:26,380
So, if our number is 1500, we shouldn't be afraid.

532
00:44:28,019 --> 00:44:33,396
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) was sending out its major caravan to Ash-Shaam(ألشام)

533
00:44:34,529 --> 00:44:41,030
The caravan was headed by Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) himself, one of the leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

534
00:44:41,815 --> 00:44:45,422
Rasool Allah ﷺ caught news of this.

535
00:44:46,165 --> 00:44:52,042
And he was sending out spies to bring him out, news of the caravan.

536
00:44:53,197 --> 00:44:57,939
So, Bisbisa Bin Amro(بسبسه بن عمرو) comes back, he enters the house of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

537
00:44:59,082 --> 00:45:03,821
Anas(انس) says, there was nobody in the house except me and Rasool Allah ﷺ and Bisbisa Bin Amro(بسبسه بن عمرو).

538
00:45:04,547 --> 00:45:10,043
And he tells Rasool Allah ﷺ that the caravan of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) was spotted, in such and such place.

539
00:45:11,024 --> 00:45:15,979
Rasool Allah ﷺ immediately comes out and says whoever has his camel ready,

540
00:45:16,019 --> 00:45:19,486
whoever has his ride ready, shall join us.

541
00:45:20,340 --> 00:45:25,609
So, some of the Sahabah said: O Rasool Ullah, our rides are in Aal-Lil-Madina(اعال المدينه)

542
00:45:25,649 --> 00:45:28,128
in a part of Madina that is a little bit far away.

543
00:45:28,331 --> 00:45:31,981
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No, you need to be ready to leave now.

544
00:45:32,299 --> 00:45:35,428
We don't have time to wait for you to go and bring your camel and come back.

545
00:45:35,936 --> 00:45:40,388
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to leave in a speedy fashion immediately.

546
00:45:40,706 --> 00:45:44,832
And therefore not enough time was given to all of the Muslims to get ready.

547
00:45:45,019 --> 00:45:50,091
So, a small number ended up going with Rasool Allah ﷺ and that number was a little over 300.

548
00:45:50,971 --> 00:45:55,660
Some say 317, Some say 319, that was it.

549
00:45:55,884 --> 00:46:00,247
The rest couldn't join because they didn't have time to prepare themselves.

550
00:46:02,008 --> 00:46:05,066
What was the purpose of this army?

551
00:46:05,557 --> 00:46:10,396
It was to take over the caravan of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) led by Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان).

552
00:46:13,016 --> 00:46:14,828
Rasool Allah ﷺ told the people;

553
00:46:15,326 --> 00:46:21,946
This caravan belongs to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and will carry much wealth, attack it may Allah present it to you.

554
00:46:23,348 --> 00:46:26,555
Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) was very careful.

555
00:46:27,508 --> 00:46:32,352
And as we mentioned earlier, Abu Jahal(ابوجهل) has already delivered warning to people of the Makkah,

556
00:46:32,410 --> 00:46:41,483
you need to be careful, your financial lines are being attacked, and your men are being attacked so, be careful.

557
00:46:41,761 --> 00:46:43,728
So, Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) was very alert.

558
00:46:44,103 --> 00:46:51,683
And he also was sending out his spies to gather news about the whereabouts of Muhammadﷺ.

559
00:46:52,869 --> 00:46:56,255
So, he reached to the place of Badr(بدر).

560
00:46:56,652 --> 00:47:00,188
Which is about 150 kilometers from Madina.

561
00:47:01,010 --> 00:47:06,130
And he holds some of the camel manure in his hand.

562
00:47:06,910 --> 00:47:13,644
And he crushes it and he said, this manure has some of the animal feed of Madina in it.

563
00:47:14,439 --> 00:47:18,427
So, he knew from the manure itself, where the camels were feeding.

564
00:47:19,359 --> 00:47:25,787
And he knew that the owners of these camels are followers of Muhammadﷺ, who are trying to pursue him.

565
00:47:26,647 --> 00:47:35,796
So, he sends very urgent to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), your caravan is being threatened, you need to come and protect it.

566
00:47:36,627 --> 00:47:40,187
He sends the message with Amr Bin Ummayyah Adh-Dhamri(عمرو بن أميه ألضمري).

567
00:47:42,539 --> 00:47:48,320
But before we talk about what Amr(عمرو) does, when he goes and delivers the warnings to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

568
00:47:48,529 --> 00:47:49,907
let's go back to Makkah.

569
00:47:51,290 --> 00:47:59,337
In Makkah, Aatiqa Bint Abdul Muttalib(عاطقه بنت عبدالمطلب), the aunt of Rasool Allah ﷺ saw a dream.

570
00:48:00,520 --> 00:48:05,313
She saw that, a man was riding his camel.

571
00:48:06,556 --> 00:48:08,988
And he rushes into Makkah.

572
00:48:09,509 --> 00:48:15,645
And he screams to gather the people of Makkah around him,

573
00:48:16,171 --> 00:48:21,250
and then his camel stands on top of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

574
00:48:22,404 --> 00:48:27,512
and then after that it stands on top of a mountain in Makkah,

575
00:48:28,663 --> 00:48:31,773
and he warns the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), he said,

576
00:48:32,537 --> 00:48:36,081
In three days, you will perish,

577
00:48:37,351 --> 00:48:41,457
and then he takes a rock and he throws it from on top of the mountain,

578
00:48:41,861 --> 00:48:46,963
it lands in the Valley of Makkah, and it explodes,

579
00:48:48,267 --> 00:48:53,574
and every house in Makkah is hit by a fragment, of this rock.

580
00:48:55,073 --> 00:49:02,773
So, she said to her brother, Al-Abbas(العباس), I'm going to tell you this dream, which has worried me.

581
00:49:03,516 --> 00:49:05,753
But I don't want you to tell anybody about it.

582
00:49:06,879 --> 00:49:10,358
Al-Abbas(العباس) listened to her narrated dream.

583
00:49:10,588 --> 00:49:15,580
And then he said that was some vision, keep quiet about it, don't tell anyone.

584
00:49:17,969 --> 00:49:23,954
Because here you have this man saying come forth to your deaths, in three days you people of perfidy.

585
00:49:25,634 --> 00:49:28,495
Now Aatiqa(عاتكه) told Al-Abbas(العباس) not to tell anybody about it.

586
00:49:29,173 --> 00:49:32,838
However, Al-Abbas(العباس) the next day finds his friend,

587
00:49:33,285 --> 00:49:38,219
his friend was Al-Waleed Bin Utba(الوليد بن عتبه) and he tells him about the dream.

588
00:49:38,259 --> 00:49:40,087
And he tells him don't tell anybody about it.

589
00:49:40,392 --> 00:49:45,617
And then Al-Waleed Bin Utba(الوليد بن عتبه) goes and tells his father, and then the news is all over Makkah

590
00:49:46,115 --> 00:49:50,096
you know, if you're not able to protect the secrets yourself, Don't expect others too.

591
00:49:51,140 --> 00:49:52,036
Al-Abbas(العباس) said;

592
00:49:52,181 --> 00:49:56,009
I arose early to make Tawaf(طواف) around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

593
00:49:56,049 --> 00:49:59,868
and there was Abu Jahal Bin Hishaam(ابوجهل بن هشام) sitting with a group of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) leaders

594
00:49:59,908 --> 00:50:03,973
and they were discussing the vision of Aatiqa(عاطقه) you know, the news was all over.

595
00:50:04,812 --> 00:50:07,229
Now, when Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) saw Al-Abbas(العباس), he told him;

596
00:50:07,229 --> 00:50:12,452
Abul Fadhal(أبو الفضل), why don't you come and join us after you finish your Tawaf(طواف).

597
00:50:12,568 --> 00:50:16,315
So, Al-Abbas(العباس) made his Tawaf(طواف) and then he went to sit with them.

598
00:50:16,654 --> 00:50:17,765
So, What does Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) say?

599
00:50:17,805 --> 00:50:18,364
He said;

600
00:50:18,555 --> 00:50:22,889
How long has your family of Abdul Muttalib(عبدالمطلب) had this female Prophet?

601
00:50:23,604 --> 00:50:26,273
So, Al-Abbas(العباس) pretends as if he doesn't know, what he's talking about.

602
00:50:26,313 --> 00:50:27,816
 He said, What do you mean?

603
00:50:28,220 --> 00:50:31,350
He said, I'm talking about the vision Aatiqa(عاطقه) saw

604
00:50:31,565 --> 00:50:37,538
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) said; Aren't you, Abdul Muttalib(عبدالمطلب)'s satisfied with having your men become Prophets,

605
00:50:37,877 --> 00:50:39,691
has it got to be your women now.

606
00:50:41,368 --> 00:50:45,606
Aatiqa(عاطقه) claims that in her vision, a man said come forth in three days.

607
00:50:46,135 --> 00:50:49,298
We're going to watch you closely for those three days.

608
00:50:49,781 --> 00:50:52,198
And if what you say is true, so be it.

609
00:50:52,444 --> 00:50:58,502
But if three days pass without nothing happening, then will judge you to be the biggest liars of all of the Arabs.

610
00:50:59,266 --> 00:51:02,660
Because in the dream, it says that come to your death in three days.

611
00:51:03,090 --> 00:51:06,693
So now, Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) is saying that three days passed by nothing happens.

612
00:51:07,024 --> 00:51:10,329
We're going to consider you the biggest liars among all the Arabs.

613
00:51:11,912 --> 00:51:15,189
So, Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) here has insulted the people of Abdul Muttalib(عبدالمطلب),

614
00:51:15,853 --> 00:51:19,431
insulted the men and insulted the women claiming that they're liars.

615
00:51:20,269 --> 00:51:21,790
Al-Abbas(العباس) went back home.

616
00:51:21,967 --> 00:51:27,893
Al-Abbas(العباس) says, that night every women of Abdul Muttalib(عبدالمطلب) came to see me and said;

617
00:51:28,173 --> 00:51:35,180
Have you agreed to let that dirty old reprobate attack first your men and then your women,

618
00:51:35,562 --> 00:51:36,604
 while you just listened.

619
00:51:37,174 --> 00:51:40,149
Didn't anything, you heard him say offend you.

620
00:51:40,488 --> 00:51:44,341
Al-Abbas(العباس) said; I would have done something but I never had a problem with him, before.

621
00:51:44,610 --> 00:51:49,043
I swear, I will confront him and if he repeats it, I'll take care of him, for you.

622
00:51:49,475 --> 00:51:54,776
So, now Al-Abbas(العباس) is charged up and he wants to take revenge from Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) for what happened.

623
00:51:55,441 --> 00:51:59,843
So, after three days, Al-Abbas(العباس) goes to Al-Haram(الحرم)

624
00:52:00,390 --> 00:52:03,966
and he wants to walk next to Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل), so that Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) would call him

625
00:52:04,343 --> 00:52:10,223
and then, he will have a chance to argue back at Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) and take revenge for what happened.

626
00:52:11,270 --> 00:52:12,886
Al-Abbas(العباس) says;

627
00:52:13,553 --> 00:52:18,386
On the morning of the third day, after Aatiqa(عاطقه)'s vision I was extremely angry

628
00:52:18,795 --> 00:52:23,565
feeling that I have let him get away with something I should have put a stop to.

629
00:52:24,489 --> 00:52:32,833
I went into the mosque and saw him, I swear I was making towards him, to confront him, to get him, to retract what he had said,

630
00:52:33,533 --> 00:52:39,069
he was a slight man with a sharp face, a sharp voice, and a sharp gaze.

631
00:52:40,213 --> 00:52:42,517
When he hurried off towards the door of the mosque.

632
00:52:42,633 --> 00:52:45,713
I asked myself, what could be the matter with the fellow

633
00:52:46,088 --> 00:52:49,036
and whether he was doing this because he feared, I was about to confront him.

634
00:52:49,076 --> 00:52:50,746
So, Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل), was running away

635
00:52:51,169 --> 00:52:53,737
Al-Abbas(العباس) thought maybe he's running away because he's afraid of me.

636
00:52:54,491 --> 00:52:57,527
But actually he had heard something, I had not

637
00:52:57,954 --> 00:53:01,513
He heard the voice of Dhamdham Bin Amr Al-Ghaffari(ضمضم بن عمرو ألغفاري)

638
00:53:01,821 --> 00:53:05,917
who was out in the center of the valley, standing by his camel.

639
00:53:06,244 --> 00:53:13,046
The man who was sent by Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) arrives three days after the dream of Aatiqa(عاطقه).

640
00:53:14,811 --> 00:53:18,376
Dhamdham Amr Al-Ghaffari(ضمضم بن عمرو ألغفاري) comes into Makkah,

641
00:53:19,366 --> 00:53:25,636
in a scene by just looking at him it was enough to strike fear in the hearts of people.

642
00:53:26,900 --> 00:53:29,736
He came in and he cut the nose of his camel.

643
00:53:30,530 --> 00:53:34,306
And he turns its saddle upside down and he tears his shirt.

644
00:53:35,268 --> 00:53:40,658
And then he stands in the middle of the valley, screaming, calling the people and saying;

645
00:53:40,698 --> 00:53:46,776
O Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) the caravan, the caravan your goods being brought by Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان)

646
00:53:46,816 --> 00:53:50,489
have been raided or waylaid by Muhammad(محمد) and his men,

647
00:53:50,685 --> 00:53:53,727
I don't think you can sa ve them, help, help.

648
00:53:54,997 --> 00:54:00,131
Al-Abbas(العباس) said and so all this diverted us both from our personal conflict.

649
00:54:00,326 --> 00:54:01,682
 Now everybody was...

650
00:54:02,473 --> 00:54:07,918
It was an emergency situation now, everyone was trying to get ready and go and defend their caravan.

651
00:54:09,837 --> 00:54:19,466
So, the people Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) mobilize to go and fight Muhammadﷺ in order to protect their caravan.

652
00:54:20,703 --> 00:54:27,318
Rasool Allah ﷺ made Shura(شورى) with the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, he said;

653
00:54:27,345 --> 00:54:28,792
اَشِيْرُوْا عَلَيْهَا يَا اَيُّهَا النَّاسْ

654
00:54:29,644 --> 00:54:31,072
Gives me counsel, O people.

655
00:54:32,111 --> 00:54:35,255
 So, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) spoke and then Umar(عُمَر) spoke.

656
00:54:36,133 --> 00:54:39,981
But it was as if Rasool Allah ﷺ wasn't really interested in, what they had to say.?

657
00:54:40,580 --> 00:54:46,601
Until Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ) said, it seems that you want us to speak, Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

658
00:54:46,673 --> 00:54:48,124
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes.

659
00:54:49,119 --> 00:54:56,535
Sa'ad(سعد) said: O Messenger of Allah, if you want us to lead our horses into the sea, we'd do so.

660
00:54:57,409 --> 00:55:03,165
And If you want us to lead our horses towards Burq-Al-Ghamaad(برق ألغماد) which is in the tip of Arabia, we'll do so.

661
00:55:04,469 --> 00:55:07,944
Go towards what Allahسبحانه وتعالى has instructed you to do.

662
00:55:08,370 --> 00:55:10,116
And that made Rasool Allah ﷺ happy.

663
00:55:10,441 --> 00:55:15,076
The reason why, Rasool Allah ﷺ wasn't interested in what Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) had to say, what Umar(عُمَر) had to say

664
00:55:15,116 --> 00:55:18,453
is because he wanted to hear what Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) had to say,

665
00:55:19,968 --> 00:55:26,702
because the Pledge of Allegiance, that was given by Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) to Rasool Allah ﷺ was to protect him.

666
00:55:27,263 --> 00:55:33,079
And this protection could imply, it could imply, doesn't necessarily imply, but it could imply

667
00:55:33,476 --> 00:55:38,124
that the protection is only within the boundaries of Madina.

668
00:55:39,211 --> 00:55:45,402
But now Rasool Allah ﷺ is leading an army and going out of Madina to raid a caravan belonging to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

669
00:55:46,116 --> 00:55:48,404
So what do the Ansaar(انصار) think about that.

670
00:55:49,516 --> 00:55:51,841
Because they could interpret the agreement that,

671
00:55:51,891 --> 00:55:57,815
they had with Rasool Allah ﷺ as saying that, this is not included in our agreement.

672
00:55:59,040 --> 00:56:02,611
So when Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ) stood up and said you can lead us wherever you want.

673
00:56:02,661 --> 00:56:06,284
If you want us to lead our horses into the ocean we'll go after you.

674
00:56:07,063 --> 00:56:09,632
And that made Rasool Allah ﷺ happy and satisfied.

675
00:56:10,130 --> 00:56:17,622
Because it shows you the protection, the understanding that the Ansaar(أنْصَار) had, of what it means, to protect Rasool Allah ﷺ.

676
00:56:17,879 --> 00:56:22,822
We are your soldiers lead us wherever you want, we will follow you.

677
00:56:24,366 --> 00:56:33,938
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ goes out and on his way he had to return, some of the Sahabah because they were too young.

678
00:56:34,992 --> 00:56:40,110
He returned Al-Baraa(ألبرآء) and he returned Abdullah Bin Umar Bin Khattabرضي الله عنه,

679
00:56:40,190 --> 00:56:44,914
so again you can contrast this with soldiers, who are defecting from their armies.

680
00:56:45,545 --> 00:56:46,580
They don't want to go and fight.

681
00:56:46,659 --> 00:56:53,517
They just want to be members of the army to take advantage of all of the freebies that they get free education and free this and free that.

682
00:56:53,957 --> 00:56:59,497
While here Rasool Allah ﷺ is dealing with people who are so eager to join him, he has turned them back.

683
00:57:01,182 --> 00:57:05,575
So, Al-Baraa(ألبرآء) was turned back, Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) was turned back, because they were too young.

684
00:57:06,810 --> 00:57:11,392
A Mushrik(مشرك) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said, I want to join you, this is a disbeliever

685
00:57:11,803 --> 00:57:13,405
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; Are you Muslim?

686
00:57:13,445 --> 00:57:14,580
 He said: no, he said;

687
00:57:14,804 --> 00:57:16,871
اِرْجِعْ فَلَا نَسْتَعِيْنَ بِمُشْرِكْ

688
00:57:17,389 --> 00:57:20,175
Go back I'm not going to seek assistance from a disbeliever.

689
00:57:20,457 --> 00:57:21,936
The man comes back again.

690
00:57:22,427 --> 00:57:24,497
Rasool Allah ﷺ tells him; Go back.

691
00:57:25,365 --> 00:57:27,961
A third time the man said; Now I'm Muslim,

692
00:57:28,142 --> 00:57:29,924
so Rasool Allah ﷺ told him to join.

693
00:57:31,865 --> 00:57:36,029
Financially the Muslims were going through a hard time,

694
00:57:36,859 --> 00:57:42,541
so every three men were sharing one camel and they would take turns.

695
00:57:43,449 --> 00:57:47,802
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was sharing just like everybody else.

696
00:57:48,584 --> 00:57:53,242
He was sharing his camel with two of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

697
00:57:53,668 --> 00:57:58,893
So, when their turn approached, they told Rasool Allah ﷺ; How about you ride and we'll walk

698
00:58:00,098 --> 00:58:08,730
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: "You are not stronger than I am, and I am in need of reward just as you are,

699
00:58:09,323 --> 00:58:15,003
مَا اَنْتُمْ بِاَقوَى مِنِّيْ وَلَا  اَنَا بِاَغْنَى عَنِ الْاَجْرِ مِنْكُمَا

700
00:58:15,748 --> 00:58:22,929
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was just like everybody else in his army, didn't treat himself with any preferential treatment.

701
00:58:23,587 --> 00:58:28,679
He was sharing his camel, just like others in the army were sharing their camel,

702
00:58:29,105 --> 00:58:33,652
and he would walk when it was his turn to walk.

703
00:58:34,944 --> 00:58:44,398
Rasool Allah ﷺ carried on towards the direction of Badr(بدر) to pursue the caravan.

704
00:58:44,787 --> 00:58:55,036
However, Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) was alerted and he was able to divert the caravan and was able to get away.

705
00:58:55,469 --> 00:59:01,410
In sha Allah Ta'ala(ان شاءالله تعالى), we'll carry on with the Battle of Badr(بدر) in our next session.

706
00:59:02,439 --> 00:59:07,185
أَقُوْلُ قَوْلِيْ هَذَا وَأَسْتَغْفِرُ اللهَ الْعَظِيْمْ وَلِيْ وَلَكُمْ فَاسْتَغْفِرُوْه’ اِنَّه هُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمْ

707
00:59:07,480 --> 00:59:12,556
وصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

708
00:59:12,786 --> 00:59:15,499
وَالسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

